WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:11.000
<v Moderator>Please prepare for the renewal of the account in front of you, as you normally would.</v>

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:27.000
<v Jordan Alvarez>Okay. First I'd look for the health score. It says 62 and amber. Why is it amber? I can't tell from here, so I'm clicking around.</v>

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:55.000
<v Jordan Alvarez>There's a Risk factors panel. That's new. Usage down, one escalation, champion changed. This is exactly what I wanted. I'd trust the score more if this was always next to it.</v>

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.000
<v Moderator>What do you expect next?</v>

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:33.000
<v Jordan Alvarez>I need the contract, open tickets and my last notes in one place. I see the renewal checklist, nice, but the tickets are only a count. I'd have to leave to read them.</v>

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:54.000
<v Jordan Alvarez>Still jumping between tabs for the support history. That's the thing I do forty times a week.</v>

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:13.000
<v Moderator>Try handing the escalation to support.</v>

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:30.000
<v Jordan Alvarez>I'm looking for a handoff button. I only see a comment box. I'd want to tag the support lead and have them see the context, not retype it.</v>

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:57.000
<v Jordan Alvarez>The playbook is rigid. It's the enterprise one, but this customer is a mid-size company, and half the steps don't apply. Can I skip steps? I'd rather adapt it.</v>

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:22.000
<v Jordan Alvarez>The customer timeline on the right is lovely. That's what I use to remember what happened. I'd keep that in the middle of everything.</v>

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:41.000
<v Moderator>How do you feel about the alerts at the top?</v>

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:55.000
<v Jordan Alvarez>Better than before, they're grouped. But I still don't know which ones matter. A priority would help.</v>

